# The 20 captured root grids (~724K of binary pickles) are NOT committed.
#
# They are deterministically regenerable with `capture_roots.py`, whose only input is the
# `environment_files/` checkout that IS committed, and `roots_manifest.json` -- which IS
# committed -- records the shape, palette and sha256 of every one. So a reader can rebuild
# them and verify byte-for-byte that they got the same grids this measurement used.
#
# Pickles are also the wrong committed format on their own terms: they are opaque to diff
# and review, and they execute on load.
roots/
